# VICTORY ROAD -- the whole road to the Pokemon League, as one walkthrough.
#
# Her words: "can you add the exit to the leag to the scanner and just pathfind from the start straight
# to it? I genuinely hate Pokemon caves." So this is not a puzzle helper. It is the entire route, from
# Nexa Town to the door into the League on 421, across nine maps.
#
# IT IS A POLICY, NOT A PATH. The first version was one path from the tile she had saved on, and her next
# report was that it "doesn't account for the fact I don't start in the cave": walk in from Nexa Town and
# she lands on one of EIGHT tiles along the bottom edge of map 412, none of which were on that path, so the
# first thing it ever said was "off the route". Now every tile she can stand on anywhere on the road --
# 24,689 of them -- carries the press that gets her to the League fastest from THERE. There is no start.
#
# Solved offline against the map files with every mechanic the road uses modelled the way the game runs it:
#
#   surfing   water tags 5 and 7. Getting ON the water is NOT a press: Events.onAction
#             (088_PokemonHiddenMoves.rb:840) wants her facing it and pressing confirm, then "Yes". So a
#             launch is its own instruction. Getting off is an ordinary press (pbEndSurf).
#   ICE       pbSlideOnIce (086_PokemonField.rb:1535): stepping onto ice carries her until the next tile is
#             impassable or not ice. A press is a whole slide, so one press can cover 20 tiles
#   ledges    pbLedge (086_PokemonField.rb:1524) jumps TWO tiles, in all four directions
#   doors     a touch-transfer fires on a BUMP when its tile is fully blocked (RMXP over_trigger?), and
#             otherwise when she steps ONTO it. Either way it is a press -- the first version took doors
#             for free from the tile beside them, so every floor ended one press short of its door.
#
# Each tile's row also names the tile that press leaves her on, so "go 12 up" is merged by following those
# links, never by searching.
#
# Not on the route, deliberately: the one push boulder on the Volcanic floor (the road goes around it),
# every side pocket, and the Hideaway, which needs Rock Climb she does not have.
